  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">One person, many surfaces</p>
    <h2>About Lawrence Winnerman</h2>
    <div class="bio-body">
      <p>
        I’m a Gen X writer and strategist based in Fort Wayne, Indiana. I spent twenty-five years in technology, including Amazon and Microsoft, where I led the global program team for the Microsoft Store Online. Then I was displaced by ageism and the first wave of AI, the same wave I now happen to be very good with. I rebuilt as an independent operator, served as COO of Blue Amp Media from 2025 to 2026, and this is the most generative run of my working life.
      </p>
      <p>
        What you’ll find here: essays on AI and work, democracy and power, and the near future; <em>Light Shines Through</em>, the first novel in The Shattered World series, serializing on <strong><em>The Hinge &amp; The Near Field</em></strong>; the podcast I co-host; and the consulting I do. Kintsugi as method, defiant joy as resistance, a small group changing the course of history.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

